hese vegetables are  for me  it's actually quite a lot i love  vegetables man like  i can have a big bowl of vegetables very  easily  but i can't because i'll bloat  i seriously think that i need to have a  cookbook because i think i'm that good  in cooking  pretty solid meal here and even though  this one is much lower in fat  her lunch more than made up with it with  the olive oil and the salmon in there so  that is  definitely fantastic but here we have a  little fat from the coconut oil  some carbs from the rice protein in the  shrimp  and lots of low fodmap veg as well  she also mentions that she loves to  marinate her shrimp in ginger to reduce  bloating and improve digestion  which may potentially help because  ginger has been shown to help speed up  stomach  emptying to help reduce indigestion now  that we've gone through the three days  let's get into our big questions is this  diet  balanced generally speaking i think it  looks pretty great chloe's calories  range from around 1700 to 2100 calories  a day  and her macronutrient distribution does  vary  quite significantly just depending on  her meals which  is fine in my books i mean that to me is  actually  usually a pretty good sign that chloe is  just listening to her body needs  which will naturally vary from day to  day we're also seeing her meet her fiber  needs without going  crazy which is advisable for somebody  struggling with  sibo and for the most part she also  seems to be meeting her micronutrient  needs as well  aside from the prebiotic vitamin c and  gut health supplements  we didn't really hear her talk a lot  about taking any other vitamins  so she may benefit from an omega-3 on  days that she's not having a rich source  like salmon  and possibly a little bit more iron and  vitamin d3  if her non-dairy milk is not fortified  but really i love that we're seeing a  nice range of protein sources from the  shrimp  to tofu to beans a variety of carbs like  rice sweet potatoes oats and noodles  