ly sensationalized titles  like  28 day flat tummy challenge and summer  shred challenge etc  in one video i saw where she was  reviewing one of her followers progress  she admitted that these are just flashy  names and that  in reality it might take people a lot  longer than  a month or whatever to get a flat tummy  we need to stop making suggestions that  anyone can get a flat tummy period  even if that means having a less  marketable program name  now in terms of commitment i will say  her programs are not  hugely overwhelming they range from 10  to 50 minutes a day  including warming up and cooling down  and a lot of them  are only half an hour long which i think  is realistic for the average user  she also has built-in rest days so i'm  happy to see that she's not telling  anyone to jump into like a two-hour  workout regime  to get supposedly shredded so all of  this is really great in my books  so generally speaking i think chloe  largely stays in her own lane  and isn't communicating really  problematic misinformation  even if the obvious focus of her channel  is on weight loss and fat loss which you  know  is not my style and that's fine i mean  this is why we have different youtubers  for different populations finally what  can we take away from chloe's channel  that we  really really like well one thing is  that on her faq of her program  she specifically encourages her  followers to not pay attention  to the scale she even mentions that  feeling stronger  more confident and happier makes a huge  difference in your everyday life  and those are things that people often  forget about  i also love when the success stories on  your instagram  are prefaced with the disclaimer to not  compare your progress  with someone else's because everyone is  different  and it's all dependent on so many  different factors  it would be really easy for her to sell  snake oil and insist that anyone who  follows her program will  drop weight really super fast but i  appreciate 